  "pass_order": [
    "ground: dark (7, 7, 40) with vivid blue clumps (24, 20, 90) on a 20 % share, from value noise stretched 4.6 × 2.6 px, so the clumps run along the scan",
    "speck field: one ranked noise field, cut at a density of 0.11 far out plus exp(−(r − 74) / 66) toward the core; far specks are blue when dim and lavender when bright, near ones gray-green, and inside 100 px they take the glow ramp, so the specks fuse into the glow",
    "glow tint: the ground under the specks greens toward the core with an 85 px e-fold, 0.55 strong, so dark ground still shows between the specks at 160 px",
    "gem: a 25 px pentagon in saturated blue with a violet face and a 2 px light rim; ten sectors out to 2.3 radii, alternate ones filled magenta or lavender with crisp 1 px edges",
    "hairlines: 4 narrow ellipses, 4 px, dark green inside the bright glow and mint outside it",
    "crayon: each orbit is 3 passes; each pass stamps the signed distance to its band edge along the ellipse at 1.1 px steps, width = 15 px × a pressure noise that runs from 0.12 to 1.2 × an end taper; for stretches the band splits into two parallel lines; each pass ends in a hook that turns about 0.8 of a turn as its curvature climbs. Ink lands where distance inside the edge + 3.6 × tooth × (paper × pressure − 0.5) clears the threshold, with the paper a 2.8 px and 1.2 px value noise plus a per-pixel draw, so the edge bites 2 to 4 px in and throws flecks out; a fine speck grain and the blue clumps then tint 15 % of stroke-core pixels; color by distance from the edge: green fringe under 2.2 px, mint to 4.5 px, a cyan core with pale blotches beyond",
    "scan line at the core's height, then 12 levels of per-pixel grain, a little bluer than neutral"
  ],
